e, and characterization of PspF, the transcriptional activator of the <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> stress-induced psp operon</article-title><source>J Bacteriol</source><year>1996</year><volume>178</volume><fpage>1936</fpage><lpage>1945</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8606168</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kesty</surname><given-names>NC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Incorporation of heterologous outer membrane and periplasmic proteins into <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> outer membrane vesicles</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2004</year><volume>279</volume><fpage>2069</fpage><lpage>2076</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14578354</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kuehn</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bacterial outer membrane vesicles and the host&#x02013;pathogen interaction</article-title><source>Genes Dev</source><year>2005</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>2645</fpage><lpage>2655</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16291643</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McBroom</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Curtiss</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Outer membrane vesicles</article-title><source>EcoSal &#x02013; Escherichia coli and Salmonella: Cellular and Molecular Biology</source><year>2005</year><publisher-loc>Washington, DC</publisher-loc><publisher-name>American Society for Microbiology Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McBroom</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Outer membrane vesicle production by <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> is independent of membrane instability</article-title><source>J Bacteriol</source><year>2006</year><volume>188</volume><fpage>5385</fpage><lpage>5392</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16855227</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McCarty</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DnaK mutants defective in ATPase activity are defective in negative regulation of the heat shock response: expression of mutant DnaK proteins results in filamentation</article-title><source>J Bacteriol</source><year>1994</year><volume>176</volume><fpage>764</fpage><lpage>780</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8300530</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Martinez</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Shed membrane microparticles from circulating and vascular cells in regulating vascular function</article-title><source>Am J Physiol Heart Circ Physiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>288</volume><fpage>H1004</fpage><lpage>H1009</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15706036</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mayrand</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biological activities of outer membrane vesicles</article-title><source>Can J Microbiol</source><year>1989</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>607</fpage><lpage>613</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2670152</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mecsas</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The activity of sigma E, an <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> heat-induci